{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3189","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3189","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3189\",\"parent_revision\":\"fa6ceb30c0f907e2556bd2ee0fcac60f7d75252e\",\"root_revision\":\"1bf62a85118b3fce097e36a38eec92d17ddcc218ab9a086a04262729f8b02f09\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Bug\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-23\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\n`backlog_core/operations.py:3702`, in `strike_entry`:\\n\\n```python\\nfor section_name, section_data in item.sections.items():\\n    if not isinstance(section_data, Section) or (section and section_name.lower() != section.lower()):\\n        continue\\n```\\n\\n`section_name` is the stored section key, which is snake_case (`acceptance_criteria`, verified in `backlog_core/tests/fixtures/issue-3152.yaml`). `section` is what the caller passes, which is the display name `backlog_view` returns \u2014 `Acceptance Criteria`.\\n\\nLowercasing both leaves `acceptance_criteria` against `acceptance criteria`. Underscore against space. The comparison never matches for any multi-word section name. Single-word sections match by coincidence, which is why the argument appears to work.\\n\\n## Impact\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nA caller that passes the `section` argument for a multi-word section skips every section, then reaches the not-found path. The error raised is `EntryNotFoundError` naming the entry ID with an empty available-IDs list \u2014 so the message blames the entry ID, which was correct, and reports that no IDs are available, which is false. The caller is directed away from the actual cause.\\n\\nThis is the second independent instance of the same mismatch \u2014 a display name compared directly against a storage key. The other is the unreachable YAML branch at `operations.py:2711`, filed separately. Both exist in a codebase that already has a section-key resolver.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Session observation during messy-read risk analysis, 2026-08-23\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-08-23\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Reproduction Not Yet Written\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z-0</sub>\\n\\nThe mechanism is established by reading the comparison and the stored key casing. A failing test has not been written. It should call `strike_entry` with a valid entry ID and the display name of a multi-word section, and assert the entry is struck \u2014 which currently raises `EntryNotFoundError` instead.\\n</div>\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z-1</sub>\\n\\nThe mechanism is established by reading the comparison and the stored key casing. A failing test has not been written. It should call `strike_entry` with a valid entry ID and the display name of a multi-word section, and assert the entry is struck \u2014 which currently raises `EntryNotFoundError` instead.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Not Established\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z-0</sub>\\n\\nWhether any caller passes `section` today. `strike_entry` searches all sections when `section` is omitted, so the defect is only reachable by callers that pass it. If no current caller does, the impact is latent rather than active \u2014 but the argument is exposed on the MCP tool surface, so any agent following the tool description can reach it.\\n</div>\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z-1</sub>\\n\\nWhether any caller passes `section` today. `strike_entry` searches all sections when `section` is omitted, so the defect is only reachable by callers that pass it. If no current caller does, the impact is latent rather than active \u2014 but the argument is exposed on the MCP tool surface, so any agent following the tool description can reach it.\\n</div>\\n\\n## User Provided Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z-0</sub>\\n\\nRouting both sides through the existing section-name resolver is the visible direction, and it is the same fix as the one for `operations.py:2711`. Whether these two should be fixed together as one change to how names are compared, or separately, is a grooming call \u2014 they share a root cause but sit on different paths, and #3188 additionally requires proving output equivalence before its branch is allowed to execute.\\n</div>\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z-1</sub>\\n\\nRouting both sides through the existing section-name resolver is the visible direction, and it is the same fix as the one for `operations.py:2711`. Whether these two should be fixed together as one change to how names are compared, or separately, is a grooming call \u2014 they share a root cause but sit on different paths, and #3188 additionally requires proving output equivalence before its branch is allowed to execute.\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"cc4bb3f4db3c0f113e85cc116d24a4a9bd068e7b0fb463b3c027637c6973702a\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABQTSEEw\"}"}